        "question": "What is Redux, and why is it used?",
        "answer": "Redux is a predictable state container for JavaScript applications. It helps manage global state in applications, making state predictable and easier to debug.",
        "keyPoints": [
            "Centralized state management.",
            "Predictable state changes using pure functions.",
            "Works well with React but can be used with other libraries.",
            "Uses actions, reducers, and a store to manage state."
