        "topic": "Redux",
        "question": "What are the core principles of Redux?",
        "answer": "Redux follows three core principles: 1) Single source of truth - The application state is stored in one central store. 2) State is read-only - The state can only be changed via actions. 3) Changes are made with pure functions - Reducers are pure functions that specify how the state should change.",
        "keyPoints": [
            "Single source of truth ensures a centralized state.",
            "State is immutable and updated only through actions.",
